- The user must be able to exit back to main menu.
- It must be clear what options the user has. 
- It must be clear where the user is.
- Spelling and grammer must be correct.

A user story can enter a sprint only when all these conditions are met:
It has a unique story ID and uses “As a…, I want…, so that…”.
Its acceptance criteria describe clear, observable behaviour and are specific enough to become unit tests.
Relevant success, failure and boundary cases are identified.
Everyone understands its scope and the whole team has agreed an estimate.
